From: Automation Platform controller <controller@pipefail.dev>
Subject: [PATCH 0001] organization deletion is an observable, resumable state machine

Implements: ADR-0001 increment 1 (CTL-041; groundwork for CTL-040)
Tested by:  awx/main/tests/unit/test_org_deletion.py (transition table, plan
            order) and the pool-manager provider-conformance leak scan against
            a deployed build.

DELETE /api/v2/organizations/N/ now returns 202 and drives an
OrganizationDeletion record through pending -> cancelling-jobs -> reaping ->
complete|failed via a dispatcherd reaper task. Active jobs are cancelled with
a bounded wait; children are deleted in dependency order (workflows,
templates, projects, inventories, notifiers, teams, labels) before the
organization row; the record survives the org (SET_NULL + snapshots) so
terminal states stay observable. A failed deletion resumes on the next
DELETE. ?mode=abort-if-active preserves the legacy refuse-while-busy
behavior. Jobs are history and are never deleted (tombstoning is increment 3).

The web tier never publishes to the dispatcher (it has no queue a worker
listens on — found live: such a publish vanishes silently). It only writes
the OrganizationDeletion row; a 20s DISPATCH_SCHEDULE pump on the task node
(process_organization_deletions) dispatches reapers for pending rows and
re-dispatches any deletion stuck non-terminal past 10 minutes, which makes
crashed reapers self-resuming by construction.

